# Local development settings. `cp dev/.env.example dev/.env`, then:
#   - docker compose (make dev-up) reads the ports and images below from dev/.env;
#   - the backend reads SOUNDINGS_* from its environment: `set -a; . dev/.env; set +a`
#     in each shell that runs `make -C backend dev`, `worker`, `migrate` or `make seed`.
# Names and meanings: backend/app/config.py and the chart (deploy/helm/README.md).
# Changed a port? Change the URLs that use it too.

# --- Dev services (docker compose) ----------------------------------------------------
SOUNDINGS_DEV_POSTGRES_PORT=5432
SOUNDINGS_DEV_KEYCLOAK_PORT=8080
SOUNDINGS_DEV_MAILPIT_UI_PORT=8025
SOUNDINGS_DEV_MAILPIT_SMTP_PORT=1025
# Images (point at an internal registry when offline).
# POSTGRES_IMAGE=postgres:16-alpine
# KEYCLOAK_IMAGE=keycloak/keycloak:26.0
# MAILPIT_IMAGE=axllent/mailpit:latest

# --- Backend ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
SOUNDINGS_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://soundings:soundings@localhost:5432/soundings
# The API (8000) and the Vite dev server (5173, proxies /api): each signs in on itself.
SOUNDINGS_BASE_URLS=http://localhost:8000,http://localhost:5173
# The "who are you?" picker, next to SSO (development only).
SOUNDINGS_DEV_LOGIN_ENABLED=true

# Single sign-on with the dev Keycloak (realm "soundings", users in dev/README.md).
# The API runs on the host, like your browser, so both use this issuer.
SOUNDINGS_OIDC_ISSUER=http://localhost:8080/realms/soundings
SOUNDINGS_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=soundings
SOUNDINGS_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=soundings-dev-secret
SOUNDINGS_OIDC_GROUPS_CLAIM=groups
# An admin-only attribute in the dev realm, as it must be (contract-phase2 section 3.3).
SOUNDINGS_OIDC_EXTERNAL_ID_CLAIM=employee_no
# Defaults: link by verified email on, auto-create off.
# SOUNDINGS_OIDC_MATCH_VERIFIED_EMAIL=true
# SOUNDINGS_OIDC_AUTO_CREATE_USERS=false

# Break-glass admin: works only while SOUNDINGS_OIDC_ISSUER is unset (comment it out to
# try it; sign in on /login with these).
SOUNDINGS_BREAK_GLASS_ENABLED=true
SOUNDINGS_BREAK_GLASS_USERNAME=admin
SOUNDINGS_BREAK_GLASS_PASSWORD=dev-break-glass-password

# Email (Phase 3) to the dev Mailpit: inbox at http://localhost:8025. The API queues
# email in the outbox; the worker sends it (`make -C backend worker` in another shell
# with this file exported). Comment out SOUNDINGS_SMTP_HOST for in-app notifications
# only (platform admins then see a banner).
SOUNDINGS_SMTP_HOST=localhost
SOUNDINGS_SMTP_PORT=1025
# none: plain SMTP (Mailpit, in-cluster relays); real servers use starttls or tls.
SOUNDINGS_SMTP_SECURITY=none
SOUNDINGS_SMTP_FROM=soundings@example.com
SOUNDINGS_SMTP_FROM_NAME="Soundings (dev)"
# Optional; Mailpit accepts any credentials, real servers get them from a Secret.
# SOUNDINGS_SMTP_REPLY_TO=innovation@example.com
# SOUNDINGS_SMTP_USERNAME=
# SOUNDINGS_SMTP_PASSWORD=
# SOUNDINGS_SMTP_CA_BUNDLE=/path/to/ca.pem   # a private CA for starttls/tls
# SOUNDINGS_SMTP_TIMEOUT=10                  # seconds, connection and each command

# Daily digests and evaluation reminders: hour and days before the due date, in this
# IANA time zone (also used for dates in emails). Defaults: UTC, 8, 2,0.
SOUNDINGS_TIMEZONE=Europe/London
# SOUNDINGS_DIGEST_HOUR=8
# SOUNDINGS_REMINDER_DAYS=2,0

# Public form, branding and PDF export (Phase 4). Customer Innovation's public form is
# on in the demo data: http://localhost:5173/customer-innovation/submit. Defaults below;
# the form's per-address limit counts every submission from your machine (one address).
# SOUNDINGS_PUBLIC_SUBMISSION_ENABLED=true
# SOUNDINGS_PUBLIC_SUBMISSIONS_PER_IP=10       # per address and hour, per API process
# SOUNDINGS_PUBLIC_SUBMISSIONS_PER_PROJECT=100 # per project and hour
# SOUNDINGS_ALTCHA_COST=5000                   # proof-of-work iterations per attempt
# SOUNDINGS_ALTCHA_EXPIRY=PT30M                # ISO 8601 duration
# SOUNDINGS_BRANDING_MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES=524288   # logo / favicon uploads
# PDF export needs Pango on this machine (Ubuntu/Debian: libpango-1.0-0
# libpangoft2-1.0-0 libharfbuzz-subset0; the image has them).

# AI assistance (Phase 6) against Soundings' fake kagent agent (dev/fake-agent: no kagent
# or model needed; dev/README.md "AI: the fake kagent"). Start it with
#   make -C dev/fake-agent run     (or: make fake-agent-image &&
#                                   docker compose -f dev/docker-compose.yml --profile ai up -d)
# then register an agent in Admin settings > AI agents and put its key in
# dev/.fake-agent-keys/<namespace>.<name> (make ai-smoke does all of it). The worker runs
# the AI runs: keep `make -C backend worker` running.
SOUNDINGS_AI_ENABLED=true
SOUNDINGS_KAGENT_URL=http://localhost:8083
SOUNDINGS_AI_MCP_URL=http://localhost:8000/mcp
# SOUNDINGS_AI_RUN_TIMEOUT=PT5M          # 30 s to 1 h
# SOUNDINGS_AI_MAX_CONCURRENT_RUNS=4     # runs at once per worker process
# SOUNDINGS_AI_AGENT_NAMESPACES=         # empty: any namespace
# SOUNDINGS_KAGENT_TOKEN=                # kagent's trusted-proxy mode (the fake's FAKE_AGENT_REQUIRE_TOKEN)
# The fake agent's host port (compose; `make -C dev/fake-agent run` uses 8083 too). It
# calls http://localhost:8000/mcp and reads keys from dev/.fake-agent-keys (git-ignored).
SOUNDINGS_DEV_FAKE_AGENT_PORT=8083
# compose only: the fake runs as this uid:gid to read the key files (yours: id -u, id -g).
# SOUNDINGS_DEV_FAKE_AGENT_USER=1000:1000
